--TEST--
`Core\Path::thisDir`'s join is added while compiling, so a join held in a variable does not compile and the help names `Core\Path::join` — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A variable is a value the program builds while it runs.
string $part = 'data';
echo Core\Path::thisDir($part), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0837]: `Core\Path::thisDir($part)` needs a relative path written as a literal
  --> case.nvs:4:25
  |
4 | echo Core\Path::thisDir($part), "\n";
  |                         ^^^^^ not a relative string literal
  = help: the folder is joined while compiling (`rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`): write a relative literal such as `'data'`, or `Core\Path::join(Core\Path::thisDir(), $part)` for a path the program builds

